    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0378" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.6463Em7/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-24T18:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 26, 4.40
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Catlin<anchor n="20" xml:id="d252-f1"/> informs me Guatemalan Government
                    declines sell Empresa Electrica<anchor n="21" xml:id="d252-f2"/> but is
                    agreeable to leasing it to his company for 10 years at $30,000.00 annual rental.
                    Mr. Catlin states he has submitted <pb facs="0379" n="294" xml:id="pg294"/> to
                    the President a lease contract along these lines which gives his company full
                    protection and preferential rights to outright purchase of plant should it be
                    sold.</p>
                <p>He states that Guatemalan officials tell him they cannot sell until outcome of
                    Paris conference is known as they do not desire to place themselves in a
                    position where Germany may demand restitution of seized German properties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d252-f1" n="20" xml:id="d252-f1-content">
                <p>Henry W. Catlin, of the Electrical Bond &amp; Share Co., New York.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d252-f2" n="21" xml:id="d252-f2-content">
                <p>See also telegram of March 29, 6 p.m., from the Chargé in Guatemala, <ref
                        target="#pg272">p. 272</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
